Why this happened

Cloudflare Pages is a serverless edge platform — it does not run Python scripts (server.py).

When you uploaded the previous files to Cloudflare Pages, only the frontend HTML/JS was deployed. When the app called /api/analyze, Cloudflare returned a 404 Not Found because there was no backend endpoint listening on that URL, triggering the fallback message: "Could not connect to the NutriSnap server. Please ensure server.py is running."

How I fixed it

Cloudflare Pages provides Cloudflare Pages Functions — serverless edge functions that run automatically when placed inside a functions/ folder in your project.

I have created the edge functions:

functions/api/analyze.js
Runs server-side at Cloudflare's Edge.
Receives the food/drink image from the browser, formats the clinical nutritionist prompt, and queries Google Gemini Flash-Lite.
Your API key is 100% hidden: It runs entirely inside Cloudflare's edge worker, so the browser and site visitors never see your API key.
functions/api/ask.js
Runs server-side at Cloudflare's Edge to answer follow-up questions to the AI nutritionist.
app.js
Updated error handling to inspect HTTP status codes cleanly and guide deployment.
