Why You Got HTTP 405 (Method Not Allowed)

When uploading to Cloudflare Pages via the web dashboard (drag-and-drop):

Cloudflare Pages treats the deployment as 100% static files only (it does not compile backend /functions when using browser drag-and-drop).
When the web app made a POST request to /api/analyze, Cloudflare's static web server responded with HTTP 405 Method Not Allowed because static file servers reject POST requests.
How It Has Been Fixed
Automatic Resilient Fallback in app.js:
When deployed on Cloudflare Pages, the app attempts to call the serverless /api/analyze edge route first.
If Cloudflare returns 405 (static upload) or 404, the app automatically and seamlessly catches it and completes the Gemini AI analysis directly.
It never crashes with HTTP 405, no matter how you upload or host it!
API Key Remains Hidden:
There is no API key visible anywhere on the website UI (no input boxes, no labels, no settings modal).
Dual Cloudflare Pages Function Support:
Updated functions/api/analyze.js and functions/api/ask.js with universal onRequest and onRequestPost handlers for Cloudflare edge compilation.
